        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodsburgh%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sits between Hewlett and Woodmere on Long Island's South Shore, bordering Brosewere Bay to the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodsburgh%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Woodsburgh is part of the Five Towns area, though not one of the five core villages, adding to its unique regional identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodsburgh%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1912, Woodsburgh celebrated its storied past, marking a milestone in its development as a resort community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
